Q1. What is SLF4J?

Interview Ready Answer

SLF4J (Simple Logging Facade for Java) is a logging facade
(abstraction layer) that provides a common logging API for different
logging frameworks such as Logback, Log4j, and java.util.logging.

It allows developers to switch logging frameworks without changing
application code.

Key Points

• Logging Facade (Not a Logging Framework).
• Provides a common logging API.
• Supports multiple logging frameworks.
• Improves flexibility.
• Widely used in Spring Boot.

======================================================================

Q2. Why do we need SLF4J?

Interview Ready Answer

SLF4J is used to decouple application code from a specific logging
framework.

It allows developers to change the logging implementation without
modifying the application's logging code.

Advantages

• Framework independent logging.
• Easy to switch logging frameworks.
• Cleaner application code.
• Better maintainability.
• Standard logging API.

