Q4. Difference between SLF4J and Log4j.

Interview Ready Answer

SLF4J

• Logging Facade.
• Provides a common logging API.
• Does not perform actual logging.
• Supports multiple logging frameworks.

------------------------------------------------------------

Log4j

• Logging Framework.
• Performs actual logging.
• Writes log messages.
• One specific implementation.

Memory Trick

SLF4J

↓

Interface / API

↓

Log4j

↓

Implementation

======================================================================

Q5. Which logging framework is used by Spring Boot?

Interview Ready Answer

Spring Boot uses Logback as the default logging framework.

Developers generally write logging code using the SLF4J API, while
Logback performs the actual logging.

